# Generated artefacts. Prettier must not touch them: the gate byte-diffs each one against
# what its generator emits, so a formatter rewriting them would make the check fail with a
# diff nobody authored -- and "the formatter did it" is indistinguishable from "the source
# changed" in a byte diff.
packages/tokens/generated/
browser/fixtures/panel-palette.css
packages/contracts/src/generated/
apps/api/config/design-tokens.php

# The same rule for the font artefacts, which `fetch-fonts.mjs` writes. ⚠ THESE WERE NOT
# LISTED, and Prettier had reformatted `fonts.css` -- rewrapping every `unicode-range` --
# so the committed file was NOT what the generator emits. Nothing caught it, because the
# fetch script needs the network and is therefore not a gate step, so there is no byte diff
# to go red. `fonts.test.ts` now asserts the equality in-process instead, which only means
# something if the formatter is out of the way.
packages/tokens/fonts/

# Fixtures that are deliberately wrong. The no-hard-coded-values rule is proven on these,
